{"title":"The AEA is making social media recommendations","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/911201861/0/marginalrevolution~The-AEA-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html","date":1737181160000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/timurkuran/status/1880124358649417876?s=61\" target=\"_blank\">Timur Kuran is right</a>, they have no business doing this.  Furthermore the quality of the work is not befitting an AEA journal.  Demonstrated preference is not stressed, for instance that even survey respondents are about <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/paulnovosad/status/1880258052429083097?s=61\" target=\"_blank\">10x more likely</a> to be reading Twitter than BlueSky.  Maybe it is all a network effect and they would prefer the other network if it were much larger, but maybe not.  Talk is cheap, especially when the AEA is surveying you.  Or maybe it is a network effect, but the dominant network cannot be broken and we should just work to improve it rather than defecting.  And did they perform his survey before the (quite significant) improvements in the X algorithm?</p>\r\n<p>Think like an economist, people!  Or should the JEL instead create a new research classification for “mood affiliation”?  Kevin Bryan <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/Afinetheorem/status/1880285108617507134\" target=\"_blank\">adds comment</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Here is youur periodic reminder that the AEA elects a president through a process that allows only one person to run for the office.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/the-aea-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html\">The AEA is making social media recommendations</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/911201861/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/911201861/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/911201861/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/911201861/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/911201861/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/911201861/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/the-aea-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/the-aea-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/the-aea-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/the-aea-is-making-social-media-recommendations.html#comment-160861777\">, even.   Title: The Cock Savior   In the dusty plains of ...</a> <i>by Windom Earle</i></li></ul></div><h3>Related Stories</h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/net-neutrality-we-hardly-knew-ye.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=net-neutrality-we-hardly-knew-ye\">Net neutrality, we hardly knew ye</a></li><li><a